 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On the Moon, a jump of just four feet nearly killed a man, and his own backpack did it.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 119
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "April nineteen seventy-two. Apollo sixteen's Charlie Duke and John Young finish their last moonwalk.",
   "from": 123,
   "to": 271
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Munich's Olympics are coming, so they invent the Moon Olympics.",
   "from": 275,
   "to": 354
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "young",
   "text": "Watch this, Charlie. I can jump flat-footed, straight up!",
   "from": 357,
   "to": 447
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Up here, you weigh one sixth as much. Young bounces like a kid.",
   "from": 450,
   "to": 546
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Duke wants to beat him. He makes a big push and flies about four feet high.",
   "from": 549,
   "to": 653
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But as he straightens up, his backpack pulls him over backward.",
   "from": 656,
   "to": 732
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "duke",
   "text": "Whoa, whoa, I can't correct it!",
   "from": 735,
   "to": 788
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He falls four feet, right onto the backpack. And that backpack is his air.",
   "from": 792,
   "to": 915
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, the Moon cuts your weight, but not your mass.",
   "from": 931,
   "to": 1015
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Duke said the pack weighed as much as he did. Once it tips, it keeps going.",
   "from": 1018,
   "to": 1112
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And it's a fiberglass shell. Crack it, and your air rushes out.",
   "from": 1116,
   "to": 1198
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "young",
   "text": "Charlie! That ain't very smart.",
   "from": 1201,
   "to": 1254
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Young helps him up. Duke freezes, listening for a hiss, a leak, anything.",
   "from": 1258,
   "to": 1370
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Nothing. The pack held.",
   "from": 1373,
   "to": 1414
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Now picture you, jumping twice as high, flipping right over.",
   "from": 1418,
   "to": 1517
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That's why moonwalkers loped and skipped, and hopped only for fun.",
   "from": 1521,
   "to": 1635
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So on the Moon, keep your jumps small. Remember the man who didn't.",
   "from": 1645,
   "to": 1756
  }
 ],
